  "description": "Habiro interpolation of the folded fibre boundary data of Sigma(2,3,5) -- the W_lambda keystone, mu-p root-cause follow-up to the LR modulus identification (#3822, single order-5 root). Extends the Hikami colored-Gauss-sum machinery to the order-2 (zeta=i) and order-3 (zeta=e^{i pi/3}) exceptional fibres and tests ONE uniform candidate interpolant F_lambda(q) = [mark lambda]^2_q / D(q)^2 (q-Verlinde measure of the affine-E8 McKay marks 1,2,3,4,5,6,4,2,3) against every computed root. STRUCTURAL REASON (not a fit): the LR colored flat amplitude factorizes |A_m^(j)(alpha)| = |A_bare|*|[alpha]_{zeta_pj^ell}| with color-INDEPENDENT bare amplitude, so the normalized squared amplitude over the McKay nodes equals [mark]^2/Sum[mark]^2 = F_lambda(zeta) EXACTLY. Sigma(2,3,5) has exactly 2 flat connections (D(2,3,5)=2, Fintushel-Stern) with rotation numbers ell_j^(m)=e_m*(30/p_j) mod p_j, E8 exponents e=1,7: orders 2,3 give ell=1 both connections (one root each), order 5 gives ell=(1,2) (the Galois pair). Four nontrivial roots + q=1; the fold changes per r (alcove {1} at p=2, {1,2} at p=3, {1,2,3,4} at p=5) -- derived, not assumed from r=5. EXACT per-root: D^2 = 4 (p2), 6 (p3), 10+-2sqrt5 (p5); F_lambda normalized (Sum=1) at every root, all in Q(sqrt5) union Z. The factorization is CONFIRMED numerically at orders 2,3 via parameter-free 2x2 amplitude inversion (ratio |A_m(alpha)|/|A_m(1)| = |[alpha]_zeta|, 40 dps, fresh-N cross-check); char-zero colors are flat-free. Archimedean F_lambda(q0) reported at both documented q0 pins with cross-pin swing -- NOT wired, mu-p tension NOT resolved. Habiro injectivity is NOT proved (class hypothesis, #3681); 4 roots + q=1 CONSTRAIN but do not UNIQUELY PIN F_lambda. No fit; nothing wired to production.",
